{"tool_name":"carna","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"carna","version":"1.3.3","home":"https://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/~will/Software/CARNA/","license":"GPL","summary":"Constraint-based Alignment of RNA Ensembles","identifiers":["biotools:carna"],"license_file":"COPYING","build":{"number":2},"requirements":{"build":["make",null],"host":["gecode 5.0.0","locarna 1.9.1"],"run":["gecode 5.0.0","locarna 1.9.1"]},"source_url":"http://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/~will/Software/CARNA/Releases/carna-1.3.3.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["carna --version"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"carna","identifiers":["biotools:carna","doi:10.1093/nar/gks491","doi:10.1007/978-3-642-15396-9_16"],"license":"GPL","summary":"Constraint-based alignment of rna ensembles","home_url":"https://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/~will/Software/CARNA/","keywords":["Internet","Nucleic Acid Conformation","RNA","Sequence Alignment","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Sequence analysis","Nucleic acid structure analysis"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"carna","home":"http://rna.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/CARNA/","summary":"Alignment of RNA structure ensembles.","addition_date":"2016-04-29T10:12:35Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-09T15:29:49Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"version":["1.2.5"],"collections":["de.NBI"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:carna","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"rna@rna.informatik.uni-freiburg.de","name":"Rolf Backofen","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-8231-3323","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"email":"rna@rna.informatik.uni-freiburg.de","name":"Rolf Backofen","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-8231-3323","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"will@bioinf.uni-leipzig.de","name":"Sebastian Will","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"email":"will@bioinf.uni-leipzig.de","name":"Sebastian Will","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"University Freiburg","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"rnateam","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://rna.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/Help.jsp"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"RNA sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3495"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"},{"term":"FASTA-like (text)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2200"}]}],"note":"CARNA requires only the RNA sequences as input and will compute base pair probability matrices and align the sequences based on their full ensembles of structures.","operation":[{"term":"Structure-based sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0294"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1916"},"format":[{"term":"ClustalW format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1982"}]},{"data":{"term":"Image","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2968"},"format":[{"term":"EPS","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3466"},{"term":"Image format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3547"},{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"}]},{"data":{"term":"Phylogenetic tree","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0872"},"format":[{"term":"newick","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1910"}]},{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"CARNA web server","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"rnateam","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gks491","metadata":{"abstract":"Due to recent algorithmic progress, tools for the gold standard of comparative RNA analysis, namely Sankoff-style simultaneous alignment and folding, are now readily applicable. Such approaches, however, compare RNAs with respect to a simultaneously predicted, single, nested consensus structure. To make multiple alignment of RNAs available in cases, where this limitation of the standard approach is critical, we introduce a web server that provides a complete and convenient interface to the RNA structure alignment tool 'CARNA'. This tool uniquely supports RNAs with multiple conserved structures per RNA and aligns pseudoknots intrinsically; these features are highly desirable for aligning riboswitches, RNAs with conserved folding pathways, or pseudoknots. We represent structural input and output information as base pair probability dot plots; this provides large flexibility in the input, ranging from fixed structures to structure ensembles, and enables immediate visual analysis of the results. In contrast to conventional Sankoff-style approaches, 'CARNA' optimizes all structural similarities in the input simultaneously, for example across an entire RNA structure ensemble. Even compared with already costly Sankoff-style alignment, 'CARNA' solves an intrinsically much harder problem by applying advanced, constraint-based, algorithmic techniques. Although 'CARNA' is specialized to the alignment of RNAs with several conserved structures, its performance on RNAs in general is on par with state-of-the-art general-purpose RNA alignment tools, as we show in a Bralibase 2.1 benchmark. The web server is freely available at http://rna.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/CARNA. \u00a9 2012 The Author(s).","authors":[{"name":"Backofen R."},{"name":"Mann M."},{"name":"Mohl M."},{"name":"Sorescu D.A."},{"name":"Will S."}],"citationCount":18,"date":"2012-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"CARNA-alignment of RNA structure ensembles"},"pmcid":"PMC3394245","pmid":"22689637","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Nucleic acid structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0097"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"CARNA web server","home":"https://bio.tools/carna","